# Credentials. The SMB user and password for the movie share live here.
.env

# Everything the portal writes about itself, and none of it belongs in a
# history: config.json rewrites on every tracked studio, every ignored scene
# and every thumbnail-size click, so committing it would bury real changes under
# thousands of noise commits — and it carries the Whisparr and TMDB keys.
#
# It is not unimportant. It holds the want list, the ignore list and the tracked
# catalogues, which nothing can regenerate. That is what the dated backups in
# backups/ are for, and why they go to the NAS as well as staying here.
config/

# The dated copies themselves.
backups/

# Node, in case a dependency ever arrives. There are none today: the whole app
# is Node stdlib, which is why there is no lockfile to commit either.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Editor and OS litter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Scratch files from a working session. Anything named _something is mine, not
# the app's — probes, one-off scripts, restores.
_*.mjs
_*.js
_*.ps1

# The template is the one env file that belongs in the repo.
!.env.example
